Description: Wayland desktop drawn as a drafting sheet
 Draftpaper is a tiling Wayland compositor whose desktop is a drafting
 sheet: there is no bar, the screen is a sheet of paper with a frame, zone
 ticks and a dot grid, and windows end exactly on the frame line. The title
 block in the corner carries the readings a bar would show (time, battery,
 power, CPU and memory, network, temperatures); the margins letter the
 workspaces, notifications and alerts, and windows can be parked in the
 side margins and brought back.
 .
 Everything is sized in millimetres of the screen. Four themes ship, and a
 theme also colours the terminal, the editor, GTK and Qt applications and
 Firefox. The session is started from the display manager ("Draftpaper");
 the live parts of the sheet are drawn with Quickshell.
